From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wuming <eva2show@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 01:22:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/11] desktop: read productName from DSH_DESKTOP_PRODUCT_NAME

The platform dotenv file owns the value like the other release settings and it defaults to 'DeepSeek Harness'. resolveDesktopProductName() names the dsh:// protocol registration, and packaging, notarization, and the packaged-runtime smoke locate '<productName>.app' through it. The macOS dsh CLI launcher reads CFBundleExecutable instead of a fixed executable name.

diff --git a/apps/desktop/cli/dsh b/apps/desktop/cli/dsh
index ee657a3d0b..cf1bf0405d 100644
--- a/apps/desktop/cli/dsh
+++ b/apps/desktop/cli/dsh
@@ -11,4 +11,5 @@ while [ -L "$launcher" ]; do
   esac
 done
 resources=$(CDPATH= cd -- "$(dirname -- "$launcher")/../../.." && pwd -P)
-ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE=1 exec "$resources/../MacOS/DeepSeek Harness" --expose-internals "$resources/app.asar/dsh/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh-desktop-host/lib/cli.js" "$@"
+executable=$(/usr/libexec/PlistBuddy -c "Print :CFBundleExecutable" "$resources/../Info.plist")
+ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE=1 exec "$resources/../MacOS/$executable" --expose-internals "$resources/app.asar/dsh/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh-desktop-host/lib/cli.js" "$@"
